   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Puzzle Snap\n\nGeometric pieces spin in from scattered positions and snap into a mark with sparks, then the wordmark slides out beside it. The mark is a fixed set of shapes; the wordmark is the text variable.\n\nCategory: logo-stings. Length: 2.2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- You have a wordmark but no animated mark, and the sting should build a simple geometric mark for you.\n- The brand is friendly or modular, and pieces clicking together tell that story.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Your real logo must appear exactly as designed: the mark here is a fixed set of shapes, so use orbit-lock or spotlight around your own logo.\n- The brand is calm or luxurious and the snapping reads as too toy-like.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Wordmark, default \"studio\"\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- primary_color (color): Primary, default \"#E5322D\"\n- secondary_color (color): Secondary, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- spark_color (color): Sparks, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- square (boolean): Square piece, default true\n- seed (number, 1-99): Seed, default 3\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Puzzle Snap\n\n  Geometric pieces spin in from scattered positions and snap into a mark with sparks, then the wordmark slides out beside it. The mark is a fixed set of shapes; the wordmark is the text variable.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/puzzle-snap/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"puzzle-snap\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2.2\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Wordmark\", \"description\": \"Wordmark that slides out beside the mark. Leave empty for the mark alone.\", \"default\": \"studio\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Stage color.\", \"default\": \"#111111\"},\n    {\"id\": \"primary_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Primary\", \"description\": \"Fill of the quarter circle and the small square.\", \"default\": \"#E5322D\"},\n    {\"id\": \"secondary_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Secondary\", \"description\": \"Fill of the dot and the wedge, and the wordmark.\", \"default\": \"#FFFFFF\"},\n    {\"id\": \"spark_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Sparks\", \"description\": \"Spark burst color.\", \"default\": \"#FFFFFF\"},\n    {\"id\": \"square\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Square piece\", \"description\": \"Include the small square piece.\", \"default\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"seed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Seed\", \"description\": \"Seed for the scattered start positions.\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 99, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.05}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Puzzle Snap</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        #root { background: var(--bg); }\n        .ps-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .ps-row { display: flex; align-items: center; }\n        .ps-svg { flex-shrink: 0; overflow: visible; }\n        .ps-word { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Inter, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.04em; color: var(--text); white-space: nowrap; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"puzzle-snap\" data-duration=\"2.2\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ps-clip\" class=\"ps-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2.2\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div class=\"ps-row\" id=\"ps-row\">\n            <svg class=\"ps-svg\" id=\"ps-svg\"></svg>\n            <span class=\"ps-word\" id=\"ps-word\"></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"puzzle-snap\";\n\nvar root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\nvar vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\nfunction num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\nfunction str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\nfunction col(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && /^#([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.test(v.trim()) ? v.trim() : f; }\nfunction bool(v, f) { return v === true || v === \"true\" ? true : v === false || v === \"false\" ? false : f; }\nvar FPS = 30;\nvar DUR = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2\");\nvar TOTAL = Math.round(DUR * FPS);\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\nfunction cl(x, a, b) { return Math.min(b, Math.max(a, x)); }\n// interpolate(x, [in...], [out...], easing): clamped on both sides, easing applied per segment.\nfunction interp(x, inp, out, easing) {\n  if (x <= inp[0]) return out[0];\n  if (x >= inp[inp.length - 1]) return out[out.length - 1];\n  var i = 0;\n  while (x > inp[i + 1]) i++;\n  var t = (x - inp[i]) / (inp[i + 1] - inp[i]);\n  if (easing) t = easing(t);\n  return out[i] + (out[i + 1] - out[i]) * t;\n}\nfunction bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n  return function (x) {\n    if (x <= 0) return 0; if (x >= 1) return 1;\n    var t = x;\n    for (var i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n      var cx = 3 * x1 * t * (1 - t) * (1 - t) + 3 * x2 * t * t * (1 - t) + t * t * t - x;\n      var d = 3 * x1 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) - 6 * x1 * t * (1 - t) + 6 * x2 * t * (1 - t) - 3 * x2 * t * t + 3 * t * t;\n      if (Math.abs(cx) < 1e-6 || Math.abs(d) < 1e-6) break;\n      t -= cx / d;\n    }\n    t = cl(t, 0, 1);\n    return 3 * y1 * t * (1 - t) * (1 - t) + 3 * y2 * t * t * (1 - t) + t * t * t;\n  };\n}\nvar E = {\n  lin: function (t) { return t; },\n  quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n  cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n  sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); }\n};\nfunction eOut(f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; }\nfunction eInOut(f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(2 * t) / 2 : 1 - f(2 - 2 * t) / 2; }; }\nvar outCubic = eOut(E.cubic), outQuad = eOut(E.quad), inCubic = E.cubic, inQuad = E.quad;\nvar inOutCubic = eInOut(E.cubic), inOutQuad = eInOut(E.quad), inOutSin = eInOut(E.sin), outSin = eOut(E.sin);\n// Damped spring from 0 to 1 (rest at 1, no initial velocity), frames at 30 fps.\nfunction spring(frame, cfg) {\n  if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n  var m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping;\n  var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m)), t = frame / FPS;\n  if (z < 1) {\n    var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n    return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n  }\n  if (z === 1) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n  var s = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + s, r2 = -z * w0 - s;\n  return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n}\n// Seeded random: same string in, same number out.\nfunction rnd(seed) {\n  var sd = String(seed), h = 1779033703 ^ sd.length;\n  for (var i = 0; i < sd.length; i++) { h = Math.imul(h ^ sd.charCodeAt(i), 3432918353); h = (h << 13) | (h >>> 19); }\n  h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 2246822507); h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 3266489909); h ^= h >>> 16;\n  var a = (h >>> 0);\n  a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n  t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n  return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n}\nfunction rgb(h) {\n  h = h.replace(\"#\", \"\");\n  if (h.length === 3) h = h[0] + h[0] + h[1] + h[1] + h[2] + h[2];\n  return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16)];\n}\nfunction mixc(a, b, t) {\n  var x = rgb(a), y = rgb(b);\n  return \"rgb(\" + Math.round(lerp(x[0], y[0], t)) + \",\" + Math.round(lerp(x[1], y[1], t)) + \",\" + Math.round(lerp(x[2], y[2], t)) + \")\";\n}\nfunction rgba(h, a) { var x = rgb(h); return \"rgba(\" + x[0] + \",\" + x[1] + \",\" + x[2] + \",\" + a + \")\"; }\nvar SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\nfunction svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n  var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n  for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n  if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n  return e;\n}\nfunction setA(e, attrs) { for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); }\n// Drive draw(frame) from the timeline; frames run 0..frames over frames/30 seconds.\nfunction drive(draw, frames) {\n  var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n  var clock = { frame: 0 };\n  tl.to(clock, { frame: frames, duration: frames / FPS, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); } }, 0);\n  draw(0);\n  return tl;\n}\nfunction finish(tl) {\n  if (tl.duration() < DUR) tl.to({}, { duration: DUR - tl.duration() });\n  tl.seek(0);\n  window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n  window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n}\n\n\nvar row = document.getElementById(\"ps-row\"), svg = document.getElementById(\"ps-svg\"), word = document.getElementById(\"ps-word\");\nvar bg = col(vars.background_color, \"#111111\"), primary = col(vars.primary_color, \"#E5322D\"), secondary = col(vars.secondary_color, \"#FFFFFF\"), sparkC = col(vars.spark_color, \"#FFFFFF\");\nvar useSquare = bool(vars.square, true), seed = Math.round(num(vars.seed, 3, 1, 99)), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0, 4);\nvar wordText = typeof vars.text === \"string\" ? vars.text : \"studio\";\nroot.style.setProperty(\"--bg\", bg); root.style.setProperty(\"--text\", secondary);\nvar W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight, s = Math.min(W, H);\nvar size = Math.round(s * 0.2), c = size / 2, gap = c * 0.08;\nvar STAGGER = 3, DRIFT = 10, SNAP = 3, SPARK = 8, SLIDE = 11;\nsvg.setAttribute(\"width\", size); svg.setAttribute(\"height\", size); svg.setAttribute(\"viewBox\", \"0 0 \" + size + \" \" + size);\nrow.style.gap = size * 0.24 + \"px\";\nword.textContent = wordText; word.style.fontSize = size * 0.5 + \"px\";\nif (!wordText) word.style.display = \"none\";\nvar u = c;\nvar pieces = [\n  { px: 0.6, py: 0.6, make: function (g) { svgEl(\"path\", { d: \"M \" + (u - gap) + \" \" + (u - gap) + \" L 0 \" + (u - gap) + \" A \" + (u - gap) + \" \" + (u - gap) + \" 0 0 1 \" + (u - gap) + \" 0 Z\", fill: primary }, g); } },\n  { px: 1.5, py: 0.5, make: function (g) { svgEl(\"circle\", { cx: u * 1.5, cy: u * 0.5, r: u * 0.36, fill: secondary }, g); } },\n  { px: 0.65, py: 1.35, make: function (g) { svgEl(\"path\", { d: \"M \" + (u - gap) + \" \" + (u + gap) + \" L \" + (u - gap) + \" \" + 2 * u + \" L 0 \" + 2 * u + \" Z\", fill: secondary }, g); } }\n];\nif (useSquare) pieces.push({ px: 1.5, py: 1.5, make: function (g) { svgEl(\"rect\", { x: u * 1.18, y: u * 1.18, width: u * 0.64, height: u * 0.64, rx: u * 0.08, fill: primary }, g); } });\npieces.forEach(function (pc, i) {\n  pc.outer = svgEl(\"g\", {}, svg);\n  pc.body = svgEl(\"g\", {}, pc.outer);\n  pc.make(pc.body);\n  pc.sparks = [];\n  for (var k = 0; k < 6; k++) pc.sparks.push(svgEl(\"line\", { stroke: sparkC, \"stroke-linecap\": \"round\", opacity: 0 }, pc.outer));\n});\nvar lastContact = (pieces.length - 1) * STAGGER + DRIFT + SNAP;\nvar rowW = row.offsetWidth;\nfunction draw(frame) {\n  var t = frame * speed;\n  var punch = spring(t - lastContact, { damping: 9, stiffness: 260, mass: 0.5 });\n  var markScale = t < lastContact ? 1 : 1 + 0.08 * (1 - punch);\n  var slide = interp(t, [lastContact + 2, lastContact + 2 + SLIDE], [0, 1], inOutCubic);\n  var reveal = interp(t, [lastContact + 4, lastContact + 4 + SLIDE], [0, 1], outCubic);\n  svg.style.transform = \"scale(\" + markScale + \")\";\n  pieces.forEach(function (pc, i) {\n    var local = t - i * STAGGER;\n    var angle = rnd(\"puzzle-snap-\" + seed + \"-\" + i + \"-a\") * Math.PI * 2;\n    var dist = s * (0.42 + 0.22 * rnd(\"puzzle-snap-\" + seed + \"-\" + i + \"-d\"));\n    var spin = (rnd(\"puzzle-snap-\" + seed + \"-\" + i + \"-r\") > 0.5 ? 1 : -1) * (120 + 160 * rnd(\"puzzle-snap-\" + seed + \"-\" + i + \"-s\"));\n    var remain = local < DRIFT ? interp(local, [0, DRIFT], [1, 0.2], outCubic) : interp(local, [DRIFT, DRIFT + SNAP], [0.2, 0], inQuad);\n    var ox = Math.cos(angle) * dist * remain, oy = Math.sin(angle) * dist * remain;\n    var pvx = pc.px * c, pvy = pc.py * c;\n    pc.body.setAttribute(\"opacity\", interp(local, [0, 3], [0, 1]));\n    pc.body.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(\" + ox + \" \" + oy + \") rotate(\" + spin * remain + \" \" + pvx + \" \" + pvy + \")\");\n    var sparkT = (local - DRIFT - SNAP) / SPARK;\n    pc.sparks.forEach(function (ln, k) {\n      if (sparkT < 0 || sparkT >= 1) { ln.setAttribute(\"opacity\", 0); return; }\n      var a = (k / 6) * Math.PI * 2 + rnd(\"puzzle-snap-\" + seed + \"-\" + i + \"-spark\") * Math.PI;\n      var e = outCubic(sparkT);\n      var r0 = c * (0.45 + 0.4 * e), r1 = r0 + c * 0.28 * (1 - 0.5 * e);\n      setA(ln, { x1: pvx + Math.cos(a) * r0, y1: pvy + Math.sin(a) * r0, x2: pvx + Math.cos(a) * r1, y2: pvy + Math.sin(a) * r1, \"stroke-width\": Math.max(1, c * 0.05 * (1 - sparkT)), opacity: 1 - sparkT });\n    });\n  });\n  if (wordText) {\n    row.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + (rowW / 2 - size / 2) * (1 - slide) + \"px)\";\n    word.style.opacity = reveal;\n    word.style.clipPath = \"inset(-30% \" + (1 - reveal) * 100 + \"% -30% -5%)\";\n    word.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + (1 - reveal) * -size * 0.3 + \"px)\";\n  }\n}\nfinish(drive(draw, TOTAL));\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
